omaboot-v: the console font of OmaBoot? Live
=============================================

omaboot-v16n, omaboot-v24n and omaboot-v32n (PSF2, 512 glyphs, 8×16, 12×24 and 16×32 px) are
our modified build of Terminus Font by Dimitar Toshkov Zhekov, made from its 'v' (512-glyph
Unicode) console set:

  - added from Terminus's CP437 'u' set: the half and shade blocks ▀ ▄ ▌ ▐ ▓, double box
    lines and a few arrows (Boot is drawn in half-block pixels);
  - added, drawn by hand in Terminus's stroke weight: a check mark ✓ (U+2713) and a filled
    triangle ▲ (U+25B2), which Terminus lacks;
  - added, drawn by the OmaBoot? authors: port symbols two cells wide (USB-A, USB-C and
    Thunderbolt 3, Thunderbolt and Mini DisplayPort, MagSafe, headphone, SD, Ethernet,
    FireWire) at private-use code points U+E200 to U+E20F, the partial mark ◐ (U+25D0,
    a circle with its left half filled) and the console key's ` drawn larger and centred
    (U+E210);
  - added, rasterised from JetBrains Mono Nerd Font (Nerd Fonts 3.5.1): 32 icons, two cells
    each, at private-use code points U+E000 to U+E03F (not the Nerd Fonts code points, which the
    Linux console can't map; see below for where they come from);
  - dropped, to stay within the console's 512-glyph limit: the rarely used Cyrillic letters
    from U+0492 up (Russian, Ukrainian, Serbian and Belarusian stay) and all of Greek
    (U+0370 to U+03FF; glyphs Greek shares with Latin, Cyrillic or symbols stay under those),
    and symbols OmaBoot? never draws: the double-line box drawing and CP437 leftovers
    (╬╪║╒╔╗╘╙╚╛╝╞╟╠╡╣╦╧╨╩ ⌐⌠⌡₧ⁿ≡∩ ♦○↕↔ ‡ ¤);
  - merged: glyphs Terminus draws identically (g and д, u and и, ù and ѝ, ɛ and ∈).

tools/font/build.py makes the current files from the previous ones.

